diff --git a/bios/patches/README.md b/bios/patches/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..37591c13
--- /dev/null
+++ b/bios/patches/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+# OpenBIOS user heap compatibility
+
+`openbios-user-heap.patch` is original compatibility source against PCSX-Redux
+commit `55fbf0468345acfbe5512628a3be5c0cfe3f22e7`, retaining its MIT license.
+Its uC-sdk submodule is `69e06871824e2d62069487a7426ded09090ceb69`.
+It changes the user allocator's complete metadata contract; it has no game
+addresses and introduces no runtime service interception. The separate kernel
+allocator remains the upstream implementation.
+
+Reproduce with a checkout of that commit and initialized `third_party/uC-sdk`:
+
+```text
+git apply /path/to/openbios-user-heap.patch
+make -C src/mips/openbios -j8
+```
+
+The verified build used PSn00bSDK 0.24's `mipsel-none-elf-gcc` 12.3.0 and GNU make
+on Windows x86-64 (MIPS tools first on PATH). The resulting openbios.bin SHA256:
+`6bee7e0b77c41ec069122127b6ec897eb7799fdf27a0bab38fb4f42424799b3d`.
+Different compilers may change the ROM layout: derive and byte-verify the ELF
+LOAD copy window and embedded shell blob again before changing a BIOS profile.
+Never retain an old compiler's empirical seed offsets without new evidence.
+
+For this build, the profile in `bios/OpenBIOS.toml` describes the proven windows.
+From the framework root, regenerate using the BIOS and shell ELFs:
+
+```text
+python tools/gen_bios_seeds_from_elf.py --profile bios/OpenBIOS.toml --elf /path/to/openbios.elf --elf /path/to/shell.elf --out recompiler/seeds/openbios_elf_seeds.json
+psxrecomp-bios --config bios/OpenBIOS.toml
+```
+
+642 symbol/data-pointer seeds plus discovery closure produce 702 functions;
+zero interpreted/skipped/unsupported; 18043 instructions; 4096 dispatch entries.
+The five old-ROM empirical offsets are superseded by this build's ELF/discovery
+proof, not merged unmodified. The title's `openbios-allocator-build.json` records
+the source patch, ELF, ROM and original homebrew probe identities.
+
+Validation: 32 directed allocator records and all heap snapshots match the
+user-supplied PSXONPSP660 reference in independent Beetle runs. This reproduces
+that reference's observable realloc metadata defect and differing exhaustion
+paths. It is directed compatibility evidence, not a proof for every BIOS
+revision or every possible heap sequence. Native Wipeout XL passes the former
+intro cleanup stall and renders its 3D credits/attract sequence.
+
+Reference firmware, generated game/BIOS C, extracted disc fixtures and captures
+remain local ignored artifacts. The supplied reference ROM is never a target
+or a package dependency.
